# Copy to deploy/.env if you need it.  Compose auto-loads .env from this
# directory.
#
# Why this exists: Aerospike ships multi-arch images, so Docker normally picks
# your host architecture and everything is fine.  But if DOCKER_DEFAULT_PLATFORM
# is set in your shell -- very common on Apple Silicon, where people set
# linux/amd64 for other projects -- it overrides the host default and you get an
# x86_64 Aerospike running under qemu without any warning.
#
# For Iteration 1 that is merely slow.  For Iteration 2 it is fatal: any
# throughput number measured under emulation is meaningless.
#
# Set this to your native platform to opt out.
#
# TMA_PLATFORM=linux/arm64
# TMA_PLATFORM=linux/amd64
